"P3370719577" "You've watched your future self rescue Mender Ramiel."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P712147809" "So as you can tell... despite what Mender Silos may have believed in the past, the Well is no mere myth. And it is not merely contained to this world, or even to this dimension.<br><br>Your efforts here will attract the attention of the Well in time, but by then it may be too late. I was sent here to accelerate that event. But becoming an Incarnate is a long, arduous, and never-ending process. It is not some switch that you flick off or on.<br><br>Even so, every journey begins with a first step."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Statesman 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page StatesmanRecluseTFBadge Text :
"P1756635648" "{HeroName}, it is... good to see you. You have been through a lot, haven't you? Serving Recluse... striking him down. We are still wary of you in the Phalanx, due to your actions against us. But, you have earned our respect for taking the fight to Recluse's door. What is it that you want from me today?"
// Answer Text :
"P1622029230" "I'm here to talk about your research on Incarnates, Positron."
// Page StatesmanTFBadge Text :
"P374461757" "{HeroName}! Always good to see you. You fought well against Recluse and his plan to absorb the powers of everyone in the world. What can I do for someone such as you?"
// Page RecluseTFBadge Text :
"P2355128108" "... {HeroName}. You need to choose your words <i>very</i> carefully. I'm not in the mood to deal with your actions any further. Unless you are here to once <i>again</i> threaten the Freedom Phalanx?"
// Answer Text :
"P3540142518" "Easy. I'm here to find out about Incarnates."
// Page Nothing Text :
"P3746243488" "{HeroName}, what can I do for you today?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P4019899130" "Incarnates? What do you want to know about them?"
// Answer Text :
"P3046634173" "I believe you might know about others becoming Incarnates."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P1858204375" "<color orange>Positron pauses, looking you over.</color><br><br> This is dangerous information, {HeroName}. You've seen what happens already when someone uses power for the wrong ends. Lord Recluse has done nothing but abuse this power. "
// Answer Text :
"P708884863" "I can handle it, Positron."
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P2173026017" "Alright, well, here is what I've found out. If you aren't careful with gaining power from the Well of the Furies, you can find yourself <i>taken over</i> by it at any time. Statesman had that problem. It's why he rarely used his full power; doing so would draw the Well's attention and force him under its control.<br><br>If you're looking for other Incarnates, I've found out that there's one named Trapdoor. Recluse did experiments on the man and forced the power of Incarnate on him.<br><br>He was captured by Arachnos, but escaped. In the process he got his hands on a powerful item, one that seems to respond to those who have the power of the Incarnate. From what I've seen, however, his Incarnate power is tainted and he can't get the item to respond to him.<br><br>If you were able to find this item, you could use it to begin your journey towards becoming an Incarnate."
// Answer Text :
"P2623672373" "Where is Trapdoor located?"
// Page Trapdoor Text :
"P2123500283" "If my latest readings are correct, he is located in a Council base. I fear the Center might be trying to use him to gain more information about Incarnates. Here's the location. I would hurry, if I were you. Someone like Trapdoor shouldn't remain in the hands of the Council.</font></color><br><br><color orange>You should go speak with Mender Ramiel about what happened here, before moving to find Trapdoor."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Recluse 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page ArbiterBadge Text :
"P758469016" "{HeroName}. I do not say this to many often, but it is good to see you, given the aid you rendered regarding that situation with Reichsman. What do you wish to speak about?"
// Answer Text :
"P3814305255" "I'm here to speak about Incarnates."
// Page UsurperBadge Text :
"P2825433215" "{HeroName}, know that the only reason I allow you to enter this hall is because of the respect you command. You are outside of my control, ever since that battle you and I had in the future.<br><br>Why have you come here today?"
// Answer Text :
"P3618646219" "It's regarding Incarnates."
// Page RecluseTFBadge Text :
"P1165751912" "Ah, {HeroName}. You're a welcome sight here within Arachnos, since your attack on the very heart of the Freedom Phalanx itself! What is it that you want?"
// Answer Text :
"P1955773778" "I want to speak with you about Incarnates."
// Page STFBadge Text :
"P1618433136" "Make this quick, {HeroName}. I have not so soon forgotten your role in stopping one of my largest plans to date."
// Answer Text :
"P1466197162" "I don't like this any more than you do. I'm here to talk to you about Incarnates."
// Page NoBadges Text :
"P2034643678" "{HeroName}. Why have you come to my doorstep? Do you wish to try to curry my favor? Or are you here to try to take my power from me?"
// Answer Text :
"P611383854" "Neither. I'm here to ask you about Incarnates."
// Page Incarnates Text :
"P4053542320" "<color orange>Lord Recluse laughs, shaking his head.</color><br><br>You've come to ask <i>me</i> about Incarnates? I suppose it is well known where the source of my power comes from.<br><br>What did you seek to know, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P4163253279" "I'm here to find out the path towards becoming an Incarnate."
// Page Page1 Text :
"P4207011102" "The path? There is no one true path, {HeroName}. Well... That isn't true. There are some ways towards becoming an Incarnate. Perhaps... You would like to offer yourself as an experiment to find out just -<br><br><color orange>Lord Recluse grips his chest as his eyes go wide.</color><br><br>Not... you...!<br><br><color orange>Recluse's head slumps forward, turning back and forth, as if struggling against something. After a moment, he calms and looks to you.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P587196211" "Recluse?"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P3168331004" "<color Gold><font outline=2>Recluse is not here at the moment. You are speaking to what many call the Well of the Furies. Recluse would never tell you what he secretly knows, what he secretly dreads. He is a... disappointment, really. He craves power, but seeks to gain it in every other method save for ones connected to myself. I can see in you this desire for power, however. You will never be able to gain it through Recluse.<br><br>That is why I am speaking to you today, {HeroName}. There are many who would stand in your way towards obtaining the power found within the Well. I would move to tip the scales in your favor. Do you know of a man named Trapdoor? He was part of Lord Recluse's plans to try to replicate my power without my actual power source. He succeeded... somewhat.<br><br>Trapdoor was recently a prisoner of Arachnos, but escaped. He tracked down an item that is connected to myself, an Incarnate artifact, if you will. He is aware of its power, but his twisted source of power will not trigger the artifact."
// Answer Text :
"P3586434815" "Where can I find Trapdoor?"
// Page Trapdoor Text :
"P2439748181" "<color Gold><font outline=2>He is hiding within a Council base, trying to escape the arm of Arachnos. If you are able to defeat him, you can claim his artifact for yourself. It will give you a link to the untapped power of the Well and begin your true rise to power. Until we meet again, {HeroName}...</font></color><br><br><color orange>The Well leaves Recluse's body. You decide it would be best to step away and speak to Mender Ramiel before pursuing the wishes of the Well."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Ramiel 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P136856507" "Have you spoken with Recluse or Positron yet?"
// Answer Text :
"P3565396468" "No, not yet."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Ramiel2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P994594487" "{HeroName}, were you able to get in touch with one of the Incarnates?"
// Answer Text :
"P1138713778" "I spoke with Recluse... and the Well."
// Answer Text :
"P466050986" "I spoke with Positron. He warned me that the Well can take over people."
// Page Recluse Text :
"P2210280039" "The Well? It communicated directly to you?<br><br><color orange>You explain to Mender Ramiel what the Well told you, along with the fate of Trapdoor.</color><br><br>Interesting... I should study more of Recluse's motives. I do wonder if he would ever be able to properly replicate the power of the Well without requiring a <i>connection</i> to it...<br><br>Oh, yes, Trapdoor. It is a bit concerning that the Well was able to take over Recluse like that. It would be a shame for you to gain this power only to lose yourself, wouldn't it? I can look into the possible reasons why this happened to Recluse. For now, I would say it's safe enough to take the artifact from Trapdoor.<br><br>The artifact is one that does not sound like it contains a lot of power. In fact, I imagine it is stilll de-powered, waiting to be activated. The sooner you can retrieve it, the better. I should have more information for you regarding this power when you return."
// Answer Text :
"P591590492" "Very well."
// Page Statesman Text :
"P1011784545" "This is very interesting, {HeroName}. My studies into the Well have not covered something such as that. I will have to expand my horizons a bit more...<br><br>You said Positron told you about a man named Trapdoor who had an artifact on him? This may be the entrance we're looking for, {HeroName}. That artifact may respond to someone such as yourself, even if its full power is not fully realized. I would propose that you go to track down the artifact, while I do my research into the Well taking control over powerful Incarnates.<br><br>You'll only need to retrieve the artifact from Trapdoor. Whether or not that's through his demise is up to you."
// Answer Text :
"P2659597953" "Alright, I'll be back soon."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Trapdoor 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P492201042" "Please... just let me walk away! I didn't want any of this to happen, I just wanted to live a normal life!"
// Answer Text :
"P1223761355" "Where is the artifact?"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P2701267632" "<color orange>You see Trapdoor grasping the artifact, glaring at you.</color><br><br>You can't have it! Do you hear me?! This holds the key to untold power, power that I won't let fall into someone else's hands!"
// Answer Text :
"P3055176390" "... you want mercy and then you say something like that?"
// Page Page3 Text :
"P1205354110" "I can't go back to my normal life, don't you understand?! I need this to continue forward, to make my mark, to fight for my old life back! I won't let <i>you</i> take away this chance from me, do you hear me?!"
// Answer Text :
"P4177734093" "I'll help you get your old life back. Just give me the artifact and you can begin."
// Answer Text :
"P3757227834" "I don’t have time for this. I'm taking this artifact, even if it's at the cost of your life!"
// Page HeroChoice Text :
"P3853222424" "You... you would do that? You're not just going to send me back to an Arachnos prison? Who could help me? Who <i>would</i> help me?"
// Answer Text :
"P3816965865" "There are people out there who will help you. Trust me."
// Page HeroChoice2 Text :
"P3873739878" "<color orange>Trapdoor looks around suspiciously, then back to you.</color><br><br>... Alright. I'll give you the artifact. But mark my words, {HeroName}. If this is a trick... If no one will help me, I'll find you again!<br><br><color orange>Trapdoor extends his hand, holding the artifact in the palm of his hand.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3515787722" "(Take the artifact)"
// Page HeroMagicOrigin Text :
"P1953513674" "<color orange>The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a magic symbol, solid in your palm.</color>"
// Page HeroMutationOrigin Text :
"P615238956" "<color orange>The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a replica DNA strand, solid in your palm.</color>"
// Page HeroNaturalOrigin Text :
"P995217371" "<color orange>The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a mirror. It is big enough that you can just see your face within it.</color>"
// Page HeroScienceOrigin Text :
"P2809398834" "<color orange>The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into an unbendable piece of paper with numerous scientific equations written on it.</color>"
// Page HeroTechOrigin Text :
"P3230451372" "<color orange>The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a schematic for some sort of device, though you're not sure what exactly this device is."
// Page VillainChoice Text :
"P2278339473" "<color orange>Trapdoor prepares to fight you again, though it's obvious that he's in no shape to pose a challenge to you anymore.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1690802410" "(Finish off Trapdoor and take the artifact)"
// Page VillainMagicOrigin Text :
"P3227211828" "<color orange>You finish off Trapdoor and rip the artifact from his hands. The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a magic symbol, solid in your palm.</color>"
// Page VillainMutationOrigin Text :
"P4006025205" "<color orange>You finish off Trapdoor and rip the artifact from his hands. The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a replica DNA strand, solid in your palm.</color>"
// Page VillainNaturalOrigin Text :
"P2016805197" "<color orange>You finish off Trapdoor and rip the artifact from his hands. The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a mirror. It is big enough that you can just see your face within it.</color>"
// Page VillainScienceOrigin Text :
"P3054133802" "<color orange>You finish off Trapdoor and rip the artifact from his hands. The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into an unbendable piece of paper with numerous scientific equations written on it.</color>"
// Page VillainTechOrigin Text :
"P138996426" "<color orange>You finish off Trapdoor and rip the artifact from his hands. The form of the artifact shifts as it rests in your hand for a few minutes before forming into a schematic for some sort of device, though you're not sure what exactly this device is."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Ramiel3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Hero Text :
"P4277370365" "I see you're back, {HeroName}, and with the artifact.<br><br>You spared Trapdoor's life in the hopes that he would live a normal life again? That's quite noble of you, I must say. It is odd, however, that the artifact changed shapes when it came into your possession. It seems to be reacting to whatever the core of your own abilities are.<br><br>Very interesting, isn't it? But we don't have time to be fascinated by things. You have a de-powered Incarnate artifact and questions about the Well. I have answers to give you to regarding both."
// Answer Text :
"P1984122306" "Ask about available missions"
// Page Villain Text :
"P3373983258" "I see you're back, {HeroName}, and with the artifact.<br><br>Trapdoor is dead then, is he? I suppose what's done is done. He made his choice, just as you made yours. What I find odd, however, is that the artifact changed shapes when it came into your possession. It seems to be reacting to whatever the core of your own abilities are.<br><br>Very interesting, isn't it? But we don't have time to be fascinated by things. You have a de-powered Incarnate artifact and questions about the Well. I have answers to give you to regarding both."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1953922737" "The power that you had in that timelime was immense, {HeroName}. We need to see about starting you down that path in order to combat what is to come.<br><br>Our best resource would be to consult with those Incarnates who currently exist among us, or someone who has been researching them. I believe you know of one Incarnate quite well, correct? Lord Recluse is one of the most 'well known' Incarnates since Statesman passed away.<br><br>However, Positron should be able to help you as well. He has been doing intense research into the nature of Incarnates ever since Statesman was killed."
// AcceptString :
"P3713209714" "Wait, well known? There are others?"
// SendOffString :
"P1780142167" "Of course. That is what I am hoping they will tell us. There are many other Incarnates out there aside from Lord Recluse. Some more powerful than them, others much less. There are even some who do not <i>realize</i> that they have this connection to the Well.<br><br>Those who are connected, however, have an acute sense of others who share this bond. Go speak with Positron to see if he will tell you what he has found regarding Incarnates."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1453074225" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: The One That Got Away</color>"

