"P185459078" "You've recovered the artifact from Trapdoor!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Villain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Statesman 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Answer Text :
"P2467711795" "I'm here to find out about Incarnates, Statesman."
// Page RecluseTFBadge Text :
"P365094840" "... {HeroName}. You had best choose your words <i>very</i> carefully. I am not in a mood to deal with your actions any further. Unless you are here to once <i>again</i> threaten the Freedom Phalanx?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P859028951" "Incarnates? What do you want to know about them? It is common knowledge where the source of my power comes from. I'm afraid, however, that there's little else I could tell you."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P2631752120" "<color orange>Statesman pauses, looking you over.</color><br><br> ... I can't divulge that information, {HeroName}. You have plenty of power already. Recluse has shown that even just <i>one</i> other powerful Incarnate is enough to throw the world into chaos. I can't risk -<br><br><color orange>Statesman begins to shake wildly, staggering backwards. After a few moments, he becomes still, breathing lightly.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1255121994" "... Statesman?"
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P3678824549" "<color Gold><font outline=2>No, not Statesman. You may know me as the Well of the Furies. I am speaking to you now through Statesman. You wish to earn my power, do you? To go beyond the limits of what your current peers are capable of? Statesman would see that no others achieve this, but I will not let his petty concerns come between you and your goals.<br><br>There is a man, his name is Trapdoor. Lord Recluse forced the powers of the Incarnate upon him, setting this man on a path that would eventually lead him to you. He had been captured by Arachnos, but escaped. In the process, he acquired a very powerful item, one that responds to those who have the power of the Incarnate.<br><br>However, his power is tainted, he is unable to get it to respond. You, however... you could obtain this item and begin your ascent to greatness. "
// Page Trapdoor Text :
"P2706783824" "<color Gold><font outline=2>He is located in a Council base, cowering in fear of his own destiny. If you go there, you can take the artifact from him and begin to move yourself forward. That is all I will say for now, {HeroName}. Until we meet again.</font></color><br><br><color orange>Statesman collapses in front of you, catching his breath. You should go speak with Mender Ramiel about what happened here, before moving to find Trapdoor."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Recluse 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Ramiel 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2735548181" "Have you spoken with Recluse or Statesman yet?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Ramiel2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Answer Text :
"P769336243" "I spoke with Statesman for a moment, before the Well took him over."
// Page Statesman Text :
"P1842895390" "Statesman was taken over by the Well? This is very interesting, {HeroName}. My studies into the Well have not covered something such as that. I will have to expand my horizons a bit more...<br><br>You said the Well told you about a man named Trapdoor who had an artifact on him? This may be the entrance we're looking for, {HeroName}. That artifact may respond to someone such as yourself, even if its full power is not fully realized. I would propose that you go to track down the artifact, while I do my research into the Well taking control over powerful Incarnates.<br><br>You'll only need to retrieve the artifact from Trapdoor. Whether or not that's through his demise is up to you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Trapdoor 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Ramiel3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P293047119" "The power that you had in that timelime was immense, {HeroName}. We need to see about starting you down that path in order to combat what is to come.<br><br>Our best resource would be to consult with those Incarnates who currently exist among us, or someone who has been researching them. I believe you know of one Incarnate quite well, correct? Lord Recluse is one of the most 'well known' Incarnates since Statesman passed away."
// AcceptString :
"P1572899137" "Well known? There are others?"
// SendOffString :
"P4054692069" "Of course. That is what I am hoping he will tell us. There are many other Incarnates out there aside from those two. Some more powerful than them, others much less. There are even some who do not <i>realize</i> that they have this connection to the Well.<br><br>Those who are connected, however, have an acute sense of others who share this bond. Go speak with Lord Recluse to see if he will tell you what they know regarding Incarnates. Just be warned, he may not be so willing to share his secrets, knowing that you may one day overshadow his current power."

